# Infinite Weblinks — environment configuration
#
# Two owner-provided values are needed to make this a fully live production
# site. Both are optional for local development and safe to leave blank; the
# app degrades safely (dev-safe booking mock; reserved .example placeholder
# origin). Neither is stored in the repo.

# 1) Booking / contact form submission endpoint.
#    Set this to a configured external form endpoint, e.g. a Formspree form URL
#    (https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxxx). When unset, the booking form uses a
#    dev-safe mock that simulates success without sending anything anywhere, and
#    a production build with no endpoint fails safe (it never claims success).
#    The PUBLIC_ prefix is required so the value reaches the client island.
PUBLIC_BOOKING_ENDPOINT=

# 2) Production site origin (absolute URL, no trailing slash), e.g.
#    https://www.infiniteweblinks.com
#    Drives absolute canonical, sitemap, robots, and Open Graph URLs. When unset,
#    a reserved https://www.infiniteweblinks.example placeholder is used (never
#    localhost) so builds stay valid; set the real domain before launch.
PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
